Left Join

Returns all records from the left most table and matching records from the right most table

Syntax:

SELECT
    jpf.job_id, 
    cd.name As company_name,
    jpf.job_title_short
FROM 
    job_postings_fact AS jpf
LEFT JOIN 
    company_dim as cd
ON  
    jpd.company_id = cd.company_id;

Right Join

Returns all records from the right most table and matching records from the left most table

INNER Join

return only when there are matches in both tables 

Full OUTER Join

Returns all rows from all tables
-If keys match, rows are combines
-If they don't, the missing side is null
Great for checking data completeness